Module 1 opens with questions managers face every day, each of which needs data:

- a **marketing research analyst** needs to assess the effectiveness of a new television advertisement;
- a **pharmaceutical manufacturer** needs to know whether a new drug is more effective than those in use;
- an **operations manager** wants to check whether product quality conforms to company standards;
- a **software company** wants to review satisfaction ratings of its call centres across the globe;
- **management** wants to assess the standard of 1st year MBA students in LMTSM.

The tools for answering such questions are **quantitative techniques**: *mathematical and statistical tools that managers use to analyse data, solve problems, and make informed decisions.* Examples on the slide: **statistical analysis, forecasting models, linear programming, decision theory and simulation**.
